#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Anything in library/ is L1 source content. A knowledge-graph reference from any artefact -- paper, L2, L3 -- resolves to it through library/."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:81
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Bind the folder name to the document's bibliography slug, so library/<bib-slug>/ and its citation key are the same string: a citation resolves to a directory without a lookup table between them."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:80
#. Diagram label
msgid "Bind the folder to its bibliography slug"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:29
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Build the L1 knowledge graph from what ingestion derived: Dublin Core, the manifest, the assets, their binding and their links."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:129
#. Diagram label
msgid "Corpus"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:47
#. Diagram label
msgid "Derived content ready"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:101
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Each reference list of the source (a References, Bibliography or Further reading section, in any of the six UN languages) becomes folio-reference/v1 nodes with the Tool references-extract: one node per cited work, provenance extracted, derivedFrom the section it was read from, and printed the entry exactly as the source prints it. Only fields read without guessing are set (address, DOI, ISBN, year, access date); a cited IRIS item the library holds gets heldAt. The nodes are the document's own bibliography on the bibliography page. A source with no reference list skips this step with nothing written."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:97
#. Diagram label
msgid "Extract reference lists"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:34
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ingestion Engine (agent, runs unattended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:26
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ingestion subprocess — build the L1 knowledge graph"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:76
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "kind / role / url-or-path / checksum / retrieved. A SIBLING of library:, never inside it: LibraryRef is regenerated from the tree, so an authored URL placed there is dropped on the next sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:118
#. Diagram label
msgid "L1 graph built"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:105
#. Diagram label
msgid "Link L1 nodes into the corpus graph"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:56
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One standalone Dublin Core record per folder. dcterms is already this corpus's JSON-LD vocabulary, so this extends a live context rather than introducing one."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:89
#. Diagram label
msgid "Read glossary and abbreviations into candidate terms"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:70
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record assets[] — local path or remote URL"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:93
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The source's glossary and abbreviations sections become candidate terms of a folio-glossary/v1 scheme with the Tool glossary-from-source, verbatim, each with source file#line, and an acronym as the notation of the term it expands. Terms a person owns are never changed, and only a person moves a term to authored. A source with no such section skips this step with nothing written."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:50
#. Diagram label
msgid "Write dublin-core.jsonld (the record of truth)"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:62
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Write manifest.jsonld for the folder: its @id, @type folio:SourceDocument, what it contains and its provenance, referencing the standalone dublin-core.jsonld as the record of truth rather than copying its fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:60
#. Diagram label
msgid "Write manifest.jsonld referencing it"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn:35
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Writes four records in a fixed order, then reads the source's glossary and reference lists into the KG, and touches the corpus graph in none of them — dublin-core as the record of truth, a manifest that references it, assets[] kept as a SIBLING of library: because that tree is regenerated and would drop anything written inside it, and finally the slug binding Task_Link depends on. A wrong order or placement is invisible until the next sync drops it."
msgstr ""
